/-
# Engel condition on involutions and derived length (Kourovka Notebook Problem 18.57)

Kourovka Notebook, Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 18.57 (D. V. Lytkina): let `G` be a finite
2-group generated by involutions in which `[x, u, u] = 1` for every `x ∈ G` and every involution `u
∈ G`. Is the derived length of `G` bounded?
-/

module

public import Batteries.Util.ProofWanted
public import Mathlib.GroupTheory.PGroup
public import Mathlib.GroupTheory.Solvable

@[expose] public section

namespace MathlibExt.GroupTheory.InvolutionEngelTwoGroupDerivedLengthKourovka18Problem57Wanted

/-!
Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka
Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 18.57 (D. V.
Lytkina). UnsolvedMath record UM-00701486 (`KOU-18.57`), dataset ulamai/UnsolvedMath v1.8.0.

`[x, u] = x⁻¹ u⁻¹ x u` and `[x, u, u] = [[x, u], u]` (replacing `x` by `x⁻¹` turns the condition for
the other commutator convention into this one). Bounded derived length means one `d` with `G⁽ᵈ⁾ = 1`
for all such groups.
-/

/-- `G` is a 2-group generated by involutions in which `[x, u, u] = 1` for every `x ∈ G` and every
involution `u`, where `[x, u] = x⁻¹ u⁻¹ x u` and `[x, u, u] = [[x, u], u]`. -/
def IsInvolutionEngelTwoGroup (G : Type) [Group G] : Prop :=
  IsPGroup 2 G ∧ Subgroup.closure {u : G | orderOf u = 2} = ⊤ ∧
    ∀ x u : G, orderOf u = 2 →
      (x⁻¹ * u⁻¹ * x * u)⁻¹ * u⁻¹ * (x⁻¹ * u⁻¹ * x * u) * u = 1

/-- Kourovka 18.57 (D. V. Lytkina): the derived length of finite 2-groups generated by involutions
with `[x, u, u] = 1` for all `x` and all involutions `u` is bounded. -/
def involutionEngelTwoGroupsBoundedDerivedLength : Prop :=
  ∃ d : ℕ, ∀ (G : Type) [Group G] [Finite G], IsInvolutionEngelTwoGroup G → derivedSeries G d = ⊥

/--
Resolved false: the Kourovka Archive answers 18.57 "No, it is not" (A. Abdollahi, 2015): such
2-groups have unbounded derived length. Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved
Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of
Solved Problems, Problem 18.57 (D. V. Lytkina); resolution: A. Abdollahi, J. Group Theory 18 (2015),
no. 1, 111-114, Kourovka Archive, Problem 18.57: No, it is not, https://arxiv.org/abs/1401.0300v49.
-/
public theorem_wanted involutionEngelTwoGroupsBoundedDerivedLength_refuted :
    ¬ involutionEngelTwoGroupsBoundedDerivedLength

end MathlibExt.GroupTheory.InvolutionEngelTwoGroupDerivedLengthKourovka18Problem57Wanted
